{:edb/db-before-t 1870 :edb/db-after-t 1871 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535183 50 #inst "2026-10-08T18:56:13.645Z" 13194139535183 true] [17592186195909 1104 #edb/ref 17592186195912 13194139535183 true] [17592186195915 1104 #edb/ref 17592186195920 13194139535183 true] [17592186195921 1104 #edb/ref 17592186195925 13194139535183 true] [17592186195926 1104 #edb/ref 17592186195929 13194139535183 true] [17592186198391 1020 #edb/ref 17592186336073 13194139535183 true] [17592186198393 1020 #edb/ref 17592186336062 13194139535183 true] [17592186198393 1020 #edb/ref 17592186336068 13194139535183 true] [17592186198769 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535183 true] [17592186198769 1100 "Describe the set $S = {5, 6, 7,..., 50}$ using a conditional definition.\n\n$N$ {{field-1}} {{field-2}} {{field-3}}" 13194139535183 false] [17592186198769 1100 "Describe the set $S={5,6,7,...,50}$ using a conditional definition.\n\n$$\nS={x\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,{{field-2}}\\le x\\le {{field-3}}}\n$$" 13194139535183 true] [17592186198769 1145 "The set $S$ contains all natural numbers between $5$ and $50$ (including $5$ and $50$).\n\nTherefore, the set can be written as\n\n$$\nS={x\\in N\\,:\\,5\\le x\\le 50}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: This definition is not unique. For example:\n\n- We can write $x\\in Z.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:\\,5\\le x\\le 50}.\n$$\n\n- We can write $4<x<51.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS={x\\in N\\,:\\,4<x<51},\n$$\n\nor, writing $x\\in Z$ as before, we have\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:\\,4<x<51}.\n$$" 13194139535183 true] [17592186198770 1017 #edb/ref 17592186195932 13194139535183 false] [17592186198770 1017 #edb/ref 17592186336056 13194139535183 true] [17592186198770 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535183 true] [17592186198770 1100 "Describe the set $S = {3, 5, 7, 9, 11,...}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n$2n + 1$ {{field-1}} {{field-2}}" 13194139535183 false] [17592186198770 1100 "Describe the set $S={3,5,7,9,11,...}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n$$\nS={{{field-1}}\\,:\\,n\\,{{field-2}}}\n$$" 13194139535183 true] [17592186198770 1145 "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n3,\\,5,\\,7,\\,11,\\,…\n$$\n\nform an arithmetic sequence with common difference $d=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =2 \\\\  & =5-3 \\\\  & =7-5 \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $n$th term ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in N,n\\ge 1$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)\\cdot d \\\\  & =3+(n-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3+2n-2 \\\\  & =2n+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS={2n+1\\,:\\,n\\in N}\n$$" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336057 13194139535183 true] [17592186336056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336058 13194139535183 true] [17592186336056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336059 13194139535183 true] [17592186336056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336060 13194139535183 true] [17592186336056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336061 13194139535183 true] [17592186336056 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535183 true] [17592186336056 1041 "field-2" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336056 1104 #edb/ref 17592186336059 13194139535183 true] [17592186336056 1110 #uuid "60f657ba-ef18-5ccd-a35d-d8b347b7116c" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336057 1034 "\\in R" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336057 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535183 true] [17592186336057 1111 #uuid "699bf6eb-29ba-5b54-a3c9-7ec84dcf1d91" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336058 1034 "\\text{is even}" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336058 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535183 true] [17592186336058 1111 #uuid "48979afb-5d74-5496-a277-2c845ad0d277" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336059 1034 "\\in N" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336059 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535183 true] [17592186336059 1111 #uuid "9872363f-9fe5-5649-a551-2d2cfa7563bc" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336060 1034 "\\text{is odd}" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336060 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535183 true] [17592186336060 1111 #uuid "9ec1448f-91b7-58b9-8b0e-94b4f5f0b536" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336061 1034 "\\in Z" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336061 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535183 true] [17592186336061 1111 #uuid "4885f03e-bc75-5736-a212-aa5e911535d9" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336062 1017 #edb/ref 17592186336063 13194139535183 true] [17592186336062 1017 #edb/ref 17592186336066 13194139535183 true] [17592186336062 1089 "q-183728" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336062 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535183 true] [17592186336062 1100 "Find the missing coefficients in the conditional definition of the set ${1,\\sqrt{2}}$ given below.\n\n${1,\\sqrt{2}}={x\\in R\\,:\\,3{x}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}\n$x\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$=0}$" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336062 1113 #uuid "b6ca7f56-21b3-5216-a2b0-306b24a6b696" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336062 1145 "The given set contains the roots $x\\in R$ of some quadratic polynomial $p(x).$\n\nSince the polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=1$ and ${x}_{2}=\\sqrt{2},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=3,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =3(x-1)(x-\\sqrt{2}) \\\\  & =3({x}^{2}-(\\sqrt{2}+1)x+\\sqrt{2}) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}-3(\\sqrt{2}+1)x+3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as follows:\n\n$$\n{1,\\sqrt{2}}={x\\in R\\,:\\,3{x}^{2}-3(\\sqrt{2}+1)x+3\\sqrt{2}=0}\n$$" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336063 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336064 13194139535183 true] [17592186336063 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336065 13194139535183 true] [17592186336063 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535183 true] [17592186336063 1041 "field-1" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336063 1104 #edb/ref 17592186336064 13194139535183 true] [17592186336063 1110 #uuid "e07b471d-78a8-5913-9810-a3bf1ddb77c0" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336064 1034 "3+3\\sqrt{2}" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336064 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535183 true] [17592186336064 1111 #uuid "4d6621c4-a07c-571d-8823-fe693d8e0a02" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336065 1034 "3" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336065 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535183 true] [17592186336065 1111 #uuid "824fad63-0ebf-5007-91c0-2a7d48c090a0" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336066 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336067 13194139535183 true] [17592186336066 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535183 true] [17592186336066 1041 "field-2" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336066 1104 #edb/ref 17592186336067 13194139535183 true] [17592186336066 1110 #uuid "e643250c-67dc-5eba-96cc-e35bb05f062c" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336067 1034 "3\\sqrt{2}" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336067 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535183 true] [17592186336067 1111 #uuid "014ec205-d1c7-569d-991e-378843824737" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336068 1017 #edb/ref 17592186336069 13194139535183 true] [17592186336068 1017 #edb/ref 17592186336071 13194139535183 true] [17592186336068 1089 "q-183729" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336068 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535183 true] [17592186336068 1100 "Find the missing coefficients in the conditional definition of the set ${-\\sqrt{3},\\sqrt{3}}$ given below.\n\n${-\\sqrt{3},\\sqrt{3}}={x\\in R\\,:\\,2{x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-1}}\n$x\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$=0}$" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336068 1113 #uuid "b30719fb-e464-5870-9e0a-b27486e0ebd9" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336068 1145 "The given set contains the roots $x\\in R$ of some quadratic polynomial $p(x).$\n\nSince the polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-\\sqrt{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=\\sqrt{3},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =2(x-(-\\sqrt{3}))(x-\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =2(x+\\sqrt{3})(x-\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =2({x}^{2}-\\sqrt{3}x+\\sqrt{3}x-(\\sqrt{3})^{2}) \\\\  & =2({x}^{2}+0x-3) \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}+0x-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as follows:\n\n$$\n{-\\sqrt{3},\\sqrt{3}}={x\\in R\\,:\\,2{x}^{2}+0x-6=0}\n$$" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336069 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336070 13194139535183 true] [17592186336069 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535183 true] [17592186336069 1041 "field-1" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336069 1104 #edb/ref 17592186336070 13194139535183 true] [17592186336069 1110 #uuid "b72edfe8-46d4-5502-8d98-484e0ba36565" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336070 1034 "0" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336070 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535183 true] [17592186336070 1111 #uuid "476194df-0b1a-5976-8cbe-4dc5fc868140" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336071 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336072 13194139535183 true] [17592186336071 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535183 true] [17592186336071 1041 "field-2" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336071 1104 #edb/ref 17592186336072 13194139535183 true] [17592186336071 1110 #uuid "736ab067-9adf-54b4-a07f-0396ff269b17" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336072 1034 "6" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336072 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535183 true] [17592186336072 1111 #uuid "035d0891-ae01-544d-aae8-24dd4104ef0f" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336073 1017 #edb/ref 17592186336074 13194139535183 true] [17592186336073 1017 #edb/ref 17592186336079 13194139535183 true] [17592186336073 1089 "q-183792" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336073 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535183 true] [17592186336073 1100 "Describe the set $S={2,1,\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{4},...}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n$$\nS={{{field-1}}\\,:\\,n\\in {{field-2}}}\n$$" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336073 1113 #uuid "f8edf910-c411-534b-97f2-739a78146702" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336073 1145 "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n2,\\,1,\\,\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\frac{1}{4},\\,…\n$$\n\nform an infinite geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=\\frac{1}{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{4}}{\\frac{1}{2}} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $n$th term ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in N,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{n-1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{n}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{-1} \\\\  & =4\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS={4\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{n}\\,:\\,n\\in N}\n$$" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336074 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336075 13194139535183 true] [17592186336074 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336076 13194139535183 true] [17592186336074 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336077 13194139535183 true] [17592186336074 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336078 13194139535183 true] [17592186336074 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535183 true] [17592186336074 1041 "field-1" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336074 1104 #edb/ref 17592186336078 13194139535183 true] [17592186336074 1110 #uuid "25c44860-4495-5018-926b-91c176bb4aec" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336075 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {2}^{n}" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336075 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535183 true] [17592186336075 1111 #uuid "1b8a2176-6f37-5bd2-b468-b232ff66f4c7" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336076 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {4}^{n}" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336076 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535183 true] [17592186336076 1111 #uuid "c29092af-c3a8-59ed-841e-9398c3d777b5" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336077 1034 "4\\cdot {2}^{n}" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336077 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535183 true] [17592186336077 1111 #uuid "49cc6f5a-fd37-5042-bedb-987180f36620" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336078 1034 "4\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{n}" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336078 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535183 true] [17592186336078 1111 #uuid "18757baa-72bd-5947-aecb-1ed04c9032a9" 13194139535183 true] [17592186336079 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336080 13194139535183 true] [17592186336079 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336